        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 189,
          "text": "Step 2: 2 orders were booked using PO only; no countersigned contract was on file at time of booking. This was"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 201,
          "text": "compliant under v1.0 but flagged as a forward-looking risk given dual-document practice trends."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 222,
          "text": "Step 3: 1 order from a customer rated C was booked without documented Finance Manager sign-off. Root cause:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 234,
          "text": "sign-off obtained verbally, not recorded in system."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 264,
          "text": "7. Prior Period Recommendations"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 288,
          "text": "- Introduce a secondary commitment document requirement beyond PO alone"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 306,
          "text": "- Enhance credit risk assessment beyond single-factor credit rating to include payment history and country risk"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 324,
          "text": "- Formalize system-based sign-off workflow to eliminate verbal approval gaps"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 354,
          "text": "8. Forward-Looking Note for Next Cycle"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 378,
          "text": "Group Finance indicated a policy update to POL-ORD-001 was planned for Q1 2025, expected to address the"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 393,
          "text": "recommendations above. The next audit cycle should re-baseline testing against the updated policy and re-assess"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 405,
          "text": "KRI-002 and KRI-003 risk ratings."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 435,
